hecks current access and original evidence and returns its exact historical reference, including after a later legitimate Review rejection; a new command still needs current eligibility.\n\nThe Import panel now exposes this narrow publication flow through the existing protected Review interface. Every warning instance and the final action require explicit confirmation. A separate IndexedDB ledger commits the original body/key before POST, keeps uncertain outcomes from creating replacement commands, and separates historical ACKs from an explicit current read. A previous page whose actor cannot be established remains read-only for an unknown outcome; a saved ACK is required for this panel’s current read. The actual synthetic browser flow loses the first successful response, replays the exact original command, and reads the real metadata/body/current afterward. This PR also adds bounded, opt-in Authoring observation for the previously unresolved browser failure: the original target click/deadline remains, but saving diagnostics may delay subsequent assertions by up to 250 ms. This observation does not identify or close the historical cause.\n\nValidation is source-specific. Service `dec1d937`: 238 related behavior tests and 55 migration tests passed, with independent Standards and Spec review. HTTP `833f0a8`: 14 publication and 30 Review HTTP tests passed; the preceding `966b6c6` had 100 projection tests and mypy over 204 source files pass, followed only by a precise fixture-body assertion correction. Both HTTP review axes found no blocking finding. Backend/observer source `62118f8` has 1028 verified engineering inputs; Web 493 tests, strict TypeScript/build, Ruff, mypy and structural spec checks passed. The one complete Python run on this source passed 2892 tests with one genuine numerical-environment skip and two dependency warnings in 956.09 seconds; the sealed calculator did not execute. The subsequently integrated UI source `4a5c6de` has 1040 verified engineering inputs and no backend delta: all 512 Web tests / 88 files, strict unused checks, TypeScript/build (754 modules), and structural spec checks passed. The isolated UI source `fa71351` had 501 Web tests and one actual synthetic browser case pass, with both independent review axes clear. These source-specific results are not a full Python or native rerun on the UI integration.\n\nThe previous public head `fb16dcc` has two terminal successful six-job CI runs, each with browser 102 passes and integration 1504 passes plus one real numerical-environment skip. These results belong to that previous source. All original failures, fixture/setup errors and source bindings remain in the evidence packages; successful later runs do not erase historical failures. New-head CI will be read independently after publication.\n\nThis remains a draft implementation PR depending on #54 and tracks #31 without closing it. The supported publisher is limited to an eligible new original text block. Generated/math/question/group/private-solution publishing, general draft editing, version comparison, review-state projection, complete impact reconciliation and content restoration remain unfinished. Test human decisions are synthetic. Production model execution and sealed numeric calculation remain unaccepted; no provider credential or paid call is included. SQL rollback is verified separately from possible unreferenced content-addressed files.\n\nEvidence is under `progress/evidence/2026-09-28/`: `M6.2-publication-service`, `M6.2-publication-http` and `M6.2-publication-combined-gates`, `M6.2-import-publication-ui`, `M6.2-import-publication-ui-combined-gates`, `M6.2-publication-portable-source-bindings`, `M6.2-authoring-observation`, and `M6.2-fb16-ci`. Portable source verification uses only named public main-history commits and exact file mappings; no auxiliary development branch is required. The sole product and engineering specification remains PRODUCT_DESIGN.md v3.0.7, SHA-256 `2d1ecce71e0aa6953c